// The files of one variable: NAME.id with its setter and getter, and
// NAME_at.id with the element setter when some script assigns an element of
// the list (an export cannot be assigned through, `(import xs)[i] = v`, so the
// write goes through a function that holds the list as a local).

exporter_variable_text(int exporter_number_variable) {
  string exporter_text_file = exporter_fill((import constant_template_set), exporter_number_variable) + "\n" + exporter_fill((import constant_template_get), exporter_number_variable);
} return string exporter_text_file;
